'analyzeBulkATACseqRLs_AllReads.sh'

   Analyze Bulk ATACseq data from pair end sequencing experiements through these steps
	1. QCs
	2. Clean Adaptors
	3. QCs after adaptors
	4. Bowtie and samtools sort
	5. Flag Stats
	6. Count MT reads
	7. Data is PE ---> $pairs\n\tFilter alignment, proper Pairs and stats
	8. Remove PCR dups and stats
	9. Intercept BlackListed regions
	11. Remove Intermediate Files, some bam also
	12. Counting reads in promoters
	13. MACS2:::params for Tn5 insert sites, params ENCODE pipe for NFRs 
	14. MACS2:::params for PE fragments TLEN  
	15. Reads in Background

   Example how to run:
	 ./1.analyzeRLs_AllReads.sh /dd_rundata/novaseq/Runs/190608_A00690_H7V22DRXX_004/Unaligned/snATAC/RL1753_2019_06_08_bulkATAC_20190527_C4593_50000nuclei_37deg_5ulTn5_S1_R1_001.fastq.gz /home/aalvarez/Bulk_ATAC_QCmetrics_tool/output > RL1753_allReads.log  2>&1 & 


'subSampling_bulkATACseq_RLs.sh'

   Dowsampling bam file, calculate and plot some statistics
	Step 1:: Calcule subsampling fractions
	Step 2:: Subsampling bam file
	Step 3:: Summarize subsampling data per RL
	Step 4:: Plots per RL	

    Example how to run:
	# Edit 3 lines of the script itself, everything explained inside and run:
	./subSampling_bulkATACseq_RLs.sh > RL1753_subSampling.log 2>&1 &



